    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\ntabline\n\n### Description\n\nmini.nvim is awesome! Thanks for all the hard work.\r\n\r\nI'm currently using the tabline module with a file-tree plugin, nvim-tree. It would be awesome if tabline could accept a number offset that pushes it to the side of the sidebar.\r\n\r\nHere are examples of other tabline plugins and their offset features\r\n* https://github.com/akinsho/bufferline.nvim#sidebar-offset\r\n* https://github.com/romgrk/barbar.nvim#integration-with-filetree-plugins\r\n\r\nThanks!",
